Research Analyst — Licensing

Copyright (C) 2026 Nrupal Akolkar <nrupalakolkar@gmail.com>

This repository is mixed-licensed: no single license covers the whole
tree. The license that applies depends on the component.

CORE ENGINE — GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later
(AGPL-3.0-or-later)

  research_analyst/    the Python engine package: analysis engines,
                       quant engine, data providers, the report
                       pipeline, CLI, API server, and TUI
  quant/               the TypeScript analytical engine (ra-quant), a
                       parity implementation of the Python quant engine
  tests/               the engine test suite (tests under ui/ belong
                       to the UI, below)
  workers/research-analyst-api/
                       the hosted API worker — it embeds the research
                       methodology and is part of the core, not
                       serving plumbing

  Full text: LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt. That file also carries the
  project's additional notice (this software is provided for
  informational and educational purposes only; it is not financial
  advice). A separate commercial license for the core is available —
  see COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md.

SCAFFOLDING AND UI — Apache License 2.0

  ui/                  the web / PWA front-end, including ui/tests/
  deploy/              deployment tooling (signed deploys, native and
                       OCI installers)
  scripts/             build, versioning, and backup glue
  .github/workflows/   CI
  workers/api-proxy/   request-routing proxy to the Python backend
  workers/backup-cron/ backup worker
  docs/, ASFQC/        documentation
  examples/            example inputs
  BUILD_PLAN.md, DEVELOPMENT_PROGRESS_TRACKER.md
  Root build and packaging files: package.json, capacitor.config.js,
  fly.toml, render.yaml, keystore.properties.template

  Full text: LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

The repository's meta-documents (this file, README.md, CHANGELOG.md,
CONTRIBUTING.md, NOTICE.md, COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md) describe the
project and this licensing split; they are not separately licensed.

Per-file license headers are being realigned to this split in a
follow-up pass. Until that pass lands, this file states the intended
licensing per component.
